{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>See, I have set before you this day life and good.</b> For if it is life you seek, look to the good — to do what is good in the eyes of HaShem. And if you say: why did he not put the good first, since through the practice of good one merits life? The answer to this is that he comes to warn him not to seek to do what is good in the eyes of HaShem in order to live, but rather to live in order to do good — that he should not seek bodily life; rather, if he seeks life, let it be so that he may be able to serve his Creator all the days of his life, as it is written (Psalms 34:13): ״מִי הָאִישׁ הֶחָפֵץ חַיִּים אֹהֵב יָמִים לִרְאוֹת טוֹב״ — for this reason he loves days, so that he may see in them the goodness of HaShem through Torah and mitzvah, as it is written immediately nearby: ״לְאַהֲבָה אֶת ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ וּלְדָבְקָה בוֹ כִּי הוּא חַיֶּיךָ״ — that is to say, this is the purpose of your life, for the Holy One, blessed be He, gives you life only for the sake of this purpose. And this is what is said here: ״לְאַהֲבָה אֶת ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ וְגוֹ׳ וְחָיִיתָ וְרָבִיתָ״ — here he put love of HaShem before ״וְחָיִיתָ וְרָבִיתָ״, whereas immediately nearby he says: ״לְמַעַן תִּחְיֶה אַתָּה וְזַרְעֶךָ, לְאַהֲבָה אֶת ה׳״ — there he put life before love of HaShem, for in truth the one depends on the other, for love of HaShem brings life; yet in any case you shall not seek life for your own needs, but only to love HaShem." "<b>And if your heart turns away.</b> That you turn your heart to idleness and do not engage all the days in the service of El, blessed be He — then ״וְנִדַּחְתָּ״, your end will be to be driven away entirely from HaShem, ״וְהִשְׁתַּחֲוִיתָ לֵאלֹהִים אֲחֵרִים״ — for idleness leads to weariness, and it removes your heart from HaShem. ״הִגַּדְתִּי לָכֶם הַיּוֹם וְגוֹ׳, לֹא תַאֲרִיכוּן יָמִים״ וְגוֹ׳ — and this is what our Sages, of blessed memory, said (Avot 3:5): one who turns his heart to idlessness is liable with his life."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:14:57.881685050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}